---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import quotes from '../../data/quotes.json';

// Only the count is sent to the client, never the quotes themselves.
const count = quotes.length;
---
<Base title="Words from the world">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Words from the world</h1>
    <p>
      These are snippets, quotes, and just some messages from people I have
      interacted with since 2021. I don't have the heart to actually remove these
      from existence, as they were all said by someone with a real life, memories,
      and everything. Although they may've forgotten that they said something, I
      have always wanted to preserve the littlest of things because it's what makes
      us human. Although some of these stem from the digital world, or even from
      real life, the connection and curiosity are what make this fascinating to me.
    </p>

    <p>Below is a list of where these messages originate from:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>h1k-collection-project (present as of: 15/04/2026)</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Rustsussy Preservation Dump (01/01/2026)</strong></li>
      <li><strong>The Global Message Board Project (19/07/2025)</strong></li>
      <li><strong>The Phase Six Contribution Section [SEC-11] (06/11/2024)</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Quotes4u Project (05/12/2023)</strong></li>
      <li><strong>Rate My Avatar Animated Board (29/09/2021)</strong></li>
    </ul>

    <blockquote id="quote">Nothing yet.</blockquote>

    <p><a href="/api/quotes/0.json" id="roll" data-count={count}>[ give me one ]</a></p>

    <pre class="invite"><code>{`The ("h1k-collection-project") will be open for a long time.
Do you want to leave a trace of yourself and anything you want here?
You know where to find me.`}</code></pre>
  </article>

  <script>
    const el = document.getElementById('quote');
    const link = document.getElementById('roll');
    const count = Number(link?.dataset.count ?? 0);
    let last = -1;

    async function roll(e: Event) {
      e.preventDefault();
      if (count < 1) return;
      let i = Math.floor(Math.random() * count);
      if (count > 1 && i === last) i = (i + 1) % count; // no repeats in a row
      last = i;
      const res = await fetch(`/api/quotes/${i}.json`);
      const data = await res.json();
      if (el) el.textContent = data.quote;
    }

    link?.addEventListener('click', roll);
  </script>
</Base>
